    "type": "game",
    "name": "MineSweeper Rush",
    "steam_appid": 3665840,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": true,
    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Introduction  </h2><br>MineSweeper Rush is a new 2D casual game that follows classic Minesweeper rules and adds new features for a fast-paced, competitive experience.  <br>The minefield grows upward continuously. When you hit a mine, the game does not end immediately\u2014instead, two new rows are quickly added.  <br>Clearing a row happens when you mark all the mines in it. If there are fewer than four rows, four new rows appear along with bonus points.  <br>As your score increases, the game speeds up. This racing element means every second counts and makes the challenge even tougher.  <br>You can choose from three modes: Easy, Normal, and Hard, or change the board size and the number of mines using shortcut keys.  <br>Your high score is recorded on one of five leaderboards so you can compare your speed and accuracy with other players.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay  </h2><br>Right-clicking a block puts a question mark on it. A block gets a flag only when it is confirmed to have a mine.  <br>You can mark a block by clicking the number next to it, and the game will automatically place flags based on the situation.  <br>Four different drag modes help you clear mines faster and score more points in less time.  <br>An AI system keeps the game fair. If no safe move exists, clicking a mine will not cause a penalty.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features  </h2><br>A built-in tutorial shows you how to play quickly, while the help menu provides clear pictures and step-by-step instructions on rules and strategies.  <br>Background music and sound effects build excitement and help you focus during the race.  <br>Six different skins are available to reduce eye strain during long, fast-paced sessions.  <br>The game window can be resized to perfectly match the board size and your screen resolution.  <br>A hidden cheat mode displays solvable blocks and automatically clears mines, making it easier to learn quick strategies.  <br>Various number display styles help you see the game state clearly, so you can plan your moves rapidly.  ",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Introduction  </h2><br>MineSweeper Rush is a new 2D casual game that follows classic Minesweeper rules and adds new features for a fast-paced, competitive experience.  <br>The minefield grows upward continuously. When you hit a mine, the game does not end immediately\u2014instead, two new rows are quickly added.  <br>Clearing a row happens when you mark all the mines in it. If there are fewer than four rows, four new rows appear along with bonus points.  <br>As your score increases, the game speeds up. This racing element means every second counts and makes the challenge even tougher.  <br>You can choose from three modes: Easy, Normal, and Hard, or change the board size and the number of mines using shortcut keys.  <br>Your high score is recorded on one of five leaderboards so you can compare your speed and accuracy with other players.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay  </h2><br>Right-clicking a block puts a question mark on it. A block gets a flag only when it is confirmed to have a mine.  <br>You can mark a block by clicking the number next to it, and the game will automatically place flags based on the situation.  <br>Four different drag modes help you clear mines faster and score more points in less time.  <br>An AI system keeps the game fair. If no safe move exists, clicking a mine will not cause a penalty.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features  </h2><br>A built-in tutorial shows you how to play quickly, while the help menu provides clear pictures and step-by-step instructions on rules and strategies.  <br>Background music and sound effects build excitement and help you focus during the race.  <br>Six different skins are available to reduce eye strain during long, fast-paced sessions.  <br>The game window can be resized to perfectly match the board size and your screen resolution.  <br>A hidden cheat mode displays solvable blocks and automatically clears mines, making it easier to learn quick strategies.  <br>Various number display styles help you see the game state clearly, so you can plan your moves rapidly.  ",
    "short_description": "MineSweeper Rush brings a fresh twist to classic Minesweeper with a growing minefield and fast row clearance. Every second counts as you race to beat your high score and climb the leaderboards.",
    "supported_languages": "English, French, Italian, German, Spanish - Spain, Danish, Ukrainian, Russian, Bulgarian, Hungarian, Indonesian, Turkish, Greek, Norwegian, Czech, Japanese, Polish, Thai, Swedish, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Romanian, Finnish, Dutch, Portuguese - Brazil, Portuguese - Portugal, Spanish - Latin America, Vietnamese, Arabic, Korean",
    "reviews": "\u201cIt's all cheap and cheerful, especially that midi music, but it's a free Minesweeper variant. I'm quite charmed by it. Feels like a freeware game I might have got off a cover disc with cheery RPS fanzine PC Gamer in the late 90s.\u201d<br>Rock Paper Shotgun<br>",
